#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068780 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068620 :question/id #uuid "ac8b39e3-a9d0-56fd-8c0b-4d748bedf7d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-5926" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb46d056a8d8010eca509543c231c875f4980a21f1af17505fa98c8c64106207.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graph of $y = \\dfrac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What is the value of $a+b+k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=-1,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=2.$ This means that $k=-1$ and $b=2,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}+(-1) = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}-1.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(3,2)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x-2}-1 \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{a}{3-2}-1 \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+k = 3+2+(-1) = 4.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "308f3685-0a90-56f3-9653-a83cec4286d2" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bc23840-5fca-5ab1-8215-29289ed3c1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067073} {:answer/id #uuid "0aee409f-813f-5b23-96f6-c8996b1d5ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067074} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca6aa37-a32c-53be-b3a8-2e8756e30847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067075} {:answer/id #uuid "3e94822c-d274-50b0-b177-bc62e7206daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067076} {:answer/id #uuid "62fe72da-ecab-5852-86f1-53bee61c0426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067077}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0ce499bd-06a0-5e9e-829b-75796d202f23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067072}] :question/id #uuid "941ea3c6-9bc1-598b-9d0e-3d2c929faac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-39046" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2c8e0ce4d8533a855c630024712be5962d09f18604ebbe013b3f929de5682e9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graph of $y = \\frac{a}{x}$. What is the value of $a$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d0fb609-e657-5fa8-aa02-1b29a6a17108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324090} {:answer/id #uuid "93df770c-7578-5cff-bcc4-9b04fad6becf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325229} {:answer/id #uuid "a644a696-298e-5cc0-be0d-ca410a4c3634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325386} {:answer/id #uuid "b41d3f18-cdf9-5fa2-b470-dcf544ed31e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325519} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f3789f-e4fd-5a42-a5cb-cb4165342690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a644a696-298e-5cc0-be0d-ca410a4c3634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325386} :answer-field/id #uuid "a82b2c51-92e6-5f97-8301-4be752819028" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a12bd3e-7b6c-59fd-a15d-349dd424b687" :question/math-academy-id "q-39047" :question/problem "![](images/01/01b742fa8f4bf42597e8653cf6b379537d95c3789743a564064a768ca343d197.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x}+k.$ What is the value of $a+k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=1.$ This means that $k=1$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}+1.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,2.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}+1 \\\\ 2.5 & =\\frac{a}{1}+1 \\\\ 1.5 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+k=1+1.5=2.5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233170 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0f171f7-913e-5612-afe3-bfe812994cbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-113479" :question/problem "![](images/65/65348161e386fac14a98e8440d32d3883b5865a6d1eecfcd58e12931730ad0b8.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What is the value of $a+b+k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=2,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=1.$ This means that $k=2$ and $b=1,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x-1}+2.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(2,5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x-1}+2 \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{a}{2-1}+2 \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+k=3+1+2=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247351 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b442222-4bb4-5441-808f-149b93f79f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244836} {:answer/id #uuid "4f201729-f2bd-5c8d-98e6-7c9d83bbae42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245017} {:answer/id #uuid "689e2ed9-c410-5bf8-9f0a-8e74ad4ed988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245239} {:answer/id #uuid "77456a39-1b73-5aa4-96a9-5745e76003d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245371} {:answer/id #uuid "980682a7-74ff-5436-a0ae-1f32094d8a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "689e2ed9-c410-5bf8-9f0a-8e74ad4ed988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245239} :answer-field/id #uuid "774573e9-555f-5a55-b0f9-b8de1dd0786c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246754}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "67f38dd1-2470-5551-aa5d-9c22a7b1ef76" :question/math-academy-id "q-113476" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c1159b59ac6a52c570852cb47ec1ef07d0985ee8b734f2e375cf54919c8b537b.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x}+k.$ What is the value of $a+k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=1.5.$ This means that $k=1.5$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}+1.5.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,3.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}+1.5 \\\\ 3.5 & =\\frac{a}{1}+1.5 \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+k=2+1.5=3.5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c45cd1-3202-543d-b101-fcb381a00caa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244477} {:answer/id #uuid "7389e644-7850-56ac-a72c-89f1d4fe23f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245346} {:answer/id #uuid "a241241f-d9d4-5867-a8a1-eec444c3e5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245762} {:answer/id #uuid "be591fb3-96fe-523f-8f8a-d8dedf511d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246010} {:answer/id #uuid "dd159692-e15b-514e-9bfe-974e05a9735a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd159692-e15b-514e-9bfe-974e05a9735a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246277} :answer-field/id #uuid "96239917-6765-55f3-abad-5af58eb4d75f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246805}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb7f3096-38d4-5d98-8011-5cb0fe69482f" :question/math-academy-id "q-113478" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f8e1c3db4120b0fcd8491a850d238b81452fb0294145a2062f96c4655164a04.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x}+k.$ What is the value of $a+k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=-1.5.$ This means that $k=-1.5$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}-1.5.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,-2)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}-1.5 \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{a}{1}-1.5 \\\\ -0.5 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+k=-0.5-1.5=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0f5357-6a5d-52cb-a0b3-8bb0331ee994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244583} {:answer/id #uuid "606311eb-894b-5b77-b109-e32e121ff8d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245155} {:answer/id #uuid "6d13ff09-b329-5200-85b0-89687a5270ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245277} {:answer/id #uuid "7f280c4b-6081-508f-8997-4749439fa6b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245435} {:answer/id #uuid "847e53f3-ba86-5571-b86e-1f4f19fe8930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "606311eb-894b-5b77-b109-e32e121ff8d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245155} :answer-field/id #uuid "917d77c5-3e45-5592-bf27-58d3f7e98794" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246797}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d881fc0-905f-5d7f-8a88-250eeb9291b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113482" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d2dec8a05bc9835693c1df9dbc54618fd39d77667cbbdcd5bb6d92bf25c0d97.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What is the value of $a+b+k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=0.5,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=3.$ This means that $k=0.5$ and $b=3,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x-3}+0.5.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,1.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x-3}+0.5 \\\\ 1.5 & =\\frac{a}{1-3}+0.5 \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{a}{-2} \\\\ a & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+k=-2+3+0.5=1.5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63ac2646-aac7-512d-bd57-05ee6c121d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63ac2646-aac7-512d-bd57-05ee6c121d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291060} :answer-field/id #uuid "001fba1b-2842-50a5-a3b7-ed1b4bf92fa0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d4cd93f-a188-5960-97b4-7d3aaab86b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d4cd93f-a188-5960-97b4-7d3aaab86b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290963} :answer-field/id #uuid "29ee49bd-0916-5d03-a69c-d3e761037ed5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291876}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3cbf4378-485f-54e7-9ce0-4301c302afe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-270750" :question/problem "![](images/07/07c9680ad2a94338bcb17c51db591eb4dc76ba483f8613bc105095a37341ebd9.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x}+k.$ What are the values of $a$ and $k?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}},$\\,k=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=1.$ This means that $k=1$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}+1.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,3.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}+1 \\\\ 3.5 & =\\frac{a}{1}+1 \\\\ 3.5 & =a+1 \\\\ a & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e157b576-33d0-51b4-8563-20ed6ac65f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e157b576-33d0-51b4-8563-20ed6ac65f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298517} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ad7797b-0ed2-5592-a64b-fb357de48495" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbd1ff2c-5fa3-5a91-966b-82862f8bef18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbd1ff2c-5fa3-5a91-966b-82862f8bef18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298628} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c8666d-0386-5757-b7ac-3a998d0e244b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7df8f515-5c51-526f-b62e-d8baea4752eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7df8f515-5c51-526f-b62e-d8baea4752eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298099} :answer-field/id #uuid "d79e9075-d93b-522f-b7af-1b7b2908431c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a1e8bac4-2103-5a0e-a08e-e356983c6103" :question/math-academy-id "q-320718" :question/problem "![](images/c9/c90af67d867e33c847f66721c1abbc6768fbc34e7f39648fbc2e4f486a87ca3f.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What are the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $k?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}},$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}},$\\,k=$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=2.5,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=-2.$ This means that $k=2.5$ and $b=-2,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x-(-2)}+2.5=\\frac{a}{x+2}+2.5.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(-5,3.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x+2}+2.5 \\\\ 3.5 & =\\frac{a}{-5+2}+2.5 \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{a}{(-3)} \\\\ a & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Some Unknowns Given the Graph of a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068813 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068655 :question/id #uuid "a76e0252-0574-520e-bb5f-43c8faf6a564" :question/math-academy-id "e-8658" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{7}{2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $y = \\dfrac{7}{2x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e8/e80865b0f32a5473da27b39537034bcdabee0a6c24032f41413e20518642d3f4.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac{7}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\dfrac{7}{2x}.$\n\n![](images/b7/b7b1fe93de798c0aa91f60f66a2507869dbe837b843b7233972e1a78ee22576a.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea2f1348-55bf-5313-8d5e-a5a097231e97" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049313 :topic/math-academy-id 2033 :topic/title "Graphing Reciprocal Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050491 :topic/math-academy-id 1252 :topic/title "Vertical Stretches of Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069099 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0116998c-47e9-5841-86c2-8a2ded661864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281698} {:answer/id #uuid "0849be28-dcef-5244-bfb5-40d2ba4f9e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e2/e2a1274fc65341a659bb76923bb69677cc33bad1b78dfdf64ba97e0c8a00fb9c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281758} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb92338-5e41-5729-abcb-0d3a4ecd399e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a3/a32495fcca947d01cf8d3218fc5cfc0cce083a34e6fb6b629d92ba9e47039a6e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282467} {:answer/id #uuid "6a015629-bc87-55cd-8426-87c48241e46c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/8974b1f9f7fe7b9b2a8ce2981bfcac086114802c8a025cd3760a9f1d73728d90.png"